  "critical_rules": [
    "Worklist title BWV578 erroneously states G major; actual key G MINOR, source guide and independent standard catalogue. Preserve raw, display corrected.",
    "BWV553/554/555/556 are among the eight unauthentic Little Preludes and Fugues BWV553-560; Bach composer asserted FALSE; do not default to J.T. Krebs or J.L. Krebs.",
    "BWV576 Fugue G major judged SPURIOUS by Grove, explicitly false Bach in Flaminio; composer unknown.",
    "BWV565 authorship is debated rather than demonstrably spurious: no surviving autograph, source Johannes Ringk; hold certainty, original violin source speculative.",
    "BWV583 posthumous organ trio copies, no autograph and conflicting designation as chorale prelude; do not force chorale collection or Bach authorship certainty.",
    "BWV966 after Reincken Hortus Musicus Sonata No.3 in IMSLP/Grove, while Flaminio says Sonata II, a source conflict to audit; distinguish Reincken original composer/Bach arranger.",
    "BWV906 Fantasia exists with unfinished fugue, c.48 surviving bars. No fabricated completed second movement.",
    "BWV552/1 opens and 552/2 closes Clavier-Übung III, with other works between; do not imply adjacent paired movements in publication.",
    "BWV539/2 is a previously staged separate documentary movement id from BWV1001 fugue, BUT entire Prelude and Fugue BWV539 is a new work candidate. Never merge movement with whole work.",
    "BWV988 aria plus thirty variations plus aria da capo forms one work (Clavier-Übung IV); BWV1087 fourteen canons related documentarily, not 14 new original source rows.",
    "BWV989 aria plus TEN variations is a different work from BWV988, despite generic name and keyboard.",
    "BWV582 passacaglia with fugue one work; passacaglia variations are internal parts.",
    "BWV903a is an early version, BWV903.2 intermediate, BWV903.3 later version of the Fantasia; versions not three separate canonical works.",
    "Six English Suites BWV806–811: source worklist has FIVE (806-809,811); BWV810 is NOT in the 50-row source extraction, but is an independently known sixth suite, only documentary if referenced.",
    "BWV 545a, 545b, 549a, 543a prior/alternate versions, with BWV545b authorship doubtful; no forced identity merge.",
    "BWV528 opening movement linked to cantata BWV76/8; some source headings split Adagio/Vivace but preserve three principal organ-trio movements.",
    "Reconstructive links limited to specific movements, version pointers, and documented originals; no transitive fanout.",
    "All 50 sources have a publicly discovered Flaminio guide; BWV529 direct access returned 429, but indexed excerpt was available. Do not claim its page was opened directly.",
    "No production graph or index changes; this closes source-coverage worklist only, NOT all audit and historical gates."
